Replace backend-built TUI catalog/selector/todo payloads with neutral canonical data and frontend-owned projections. Cover slash-command and file-reference catalogs and generations, model/reasoning/scoped-model choices, session and user-turn pickers, theme/settings choices where not already migrated, todos and workspace metadata. Inspect app/tui catalog/keybinding adapters, interactive_tui.cpp callback builders, runtime_views.*, composer presentation types and selector tests. Formatting, filtering, current highlight and scroll state belong to the frontend; permissioned discovery, source authority and persistent selection mutations remain backend-owned.

Preserve existing generation-based avoidance of repeated catalog work and explicit unknown/loading/error/empty distinctions. Large lists must not be recopied or rebuilt on every render; copy under bounded locks and derive expensive presentation outside those locks. Selector actions carry opaque identifiers validated by the backend and publish resulting state through UnlockedData; they do not return SelectListView or another replacement UI bundle. A selector refresh must preserve selection when valid and invalidate it safely when the underlying entry disappears or a session changes.

Remove each obsolete callback-returned state view and initial snapshot field as migrated. Verify catalog generations, no-op refreshes, discovery failures, stale selections, scoped-model bulk actions, session sorting/filtering/archive/branch navigation, todos and user-turn fork/copy authorization. Run selector/completion/render tests and terminal model-selector/slash-completion/session-picker scenarios. No backend authority or hidden session source path may become a frontend cache merely to simplify the migration.
